# Template for the one secret the sieve tooling reads: SIEVE_API_KEY.
#
# Where it belongs now: Infisical, not a file on your disk. See SECRETS.md for the
# migration and the daily workflow. Start the tooling through the CLI instead of a
# dotenv file:
#
#   infisical run --env=dev -- python tools/sieve_run.py run "Extract ..."
#
# so the key arrives as an environment variable and no .env is read at all.
#
# This file stays tracked and secret-free and keeps two jobs:
#   1. a template, if you must bootstrap a key before Infisical is set up
#   2. a hand-editable reference for exactly what the tooling reads
#
# `python tools/sieve_run.py login` still writes SIEVE_API_KEY into .env as a
# bootstrap. That is the file to drag onto the Infisical Secrets Overview page to
# import the key; delete the local copy once Infisical serves it. .env is
# gitignored - never commit a real key, and never let one reach a built page, a
# log line, an error report, or stage output.

SIEVE_API_KEY=

# Optional. Overrides the API host for local tests or a self-hosted deployment.
# Leave unset in normal use; the client already defaults to the production host.
# SIEVE_BASE_URL=https://scrape.usesieve.com
